{
  "kind": "walk8",
  "comment": "Pose guides for the 8-direction, 8-frame walk sheet; same normalised cell space as idle8.json (x and y run 0..1 across one cell, y down), and the same five authored directions -- front, front_left, left, back_left, back -- with the three right-hand ones derived by the `mirror` key. The cycle is the legacy walk.json order at double resolution: contact, down, passing, up, then the same four with the other leg leading, so frames 0 and 4 are the two contacts and the body sits lowest on 1 and 5 and highest on 3 and 7. Arms swing against their own leg and hang on the hip line rather than ahead of it, which is the one thing the shipped Troupe keys get wrong. The front and back rows use a much smaller stride than the profile rows on purpose: a stride drawn towards the camera reads as a stumble, so those rows carry the cycle in the body bob, the lifted foot, a little lateral spread of the reaching leg and a near/far offset that keeps the two contacts apart. front_left and back_left carry the same points, and so do front and back, for turnaround.json's reason: a stick figure cannot say which way a body faces once the limbs are placed.",
